      "age_rating": "All Ages",
      "note": null,
      "description": "Born on March 10, 1993, a “Grady Baby” from Atlanta’s southside, Hitchcock began rapping at 12, sharpening his skills through freestyles and early mixtapes. While attending Georgia Southern University as a pre-med student, he launched his New Atlanta Tuesdays freestyle series, viral dorm-room videos that ultimately pushed him to leave school and pursue music full-time. That leap resulted in a steady run of independent projects, including 19 Summers (2012), Wishful Thinking (2015), Good (2016), and So Much for Good Luck (2017), each sharpening his reputation as a thoughtful and technically gifted MC."
